==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|lang=fr|bigot||a bigot, hypocrite}}, from {{etyl|frm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lang=fro|bigot}}, a derogatory term applied to Normans for their frequent note of the {{etyl|ang}} oath {{term||bī god|lang=ang}} "{{l|en|by God}}".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbɪɡət/}}, {{SAMPA|/"bIg@t/}}, {{enPR|bĭgʹət}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is obstinately or [[intolerant]]ly devoted to his or her own opinions and [[prejudice]]s.
# One who is strongly [[partial]] to one's own [[group]], [[religion]], [[race]], or [[politics]] and is [[intolerant]] of those who differ.

====Derived terms====
* [[bigoted]]
* [[bigotry]]

